Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `keep` takes `v`, but `v` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/lambda_call_after_capture_moved.jet:10:16
    |
 10 |     print(keep(v))
    |                ^
  --> tests/ui/lambda_call_after_capture_moved.jet:11:5
    |
 11 |     add()
    |     ^^^ `v` is used again here
 Why: `keep` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `v` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `v.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `v`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `v`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209

